Native 60 FPS: the camera update keeps the 30 Hz script step.

Reported: at 60 FPS the skull platform in Air Crash sends the camera back to
the start of the level, where it stays. The platform ends the secret
jet-board section (zones S3-S9, S0). Its warp is a handshake with the camera:
Crash's state 65 spins, fades to black and queues camera event 0x10; S0's end
record turns that into a prepared cut to zone 04, which sends Crash the
teleport (event 0x3200, state 39) that queues "cut now". The camera follows
its path meanwhile, a step per call (0x80023E60) with no frame-time term, so
once per field it moved twice as far - and S0's end links into zones 03/04,
the level's start. A camera that leaves S0 before the fade ends finds no 0x10
record: no cut, no teleport.

crash2_60fps.h:
- the camera update (0x80026CA0) runs on script steps only: its entry hook
  stores the crash pointer (step) or 0 (physics-only field) at sp+44 of the
  48-byte frame, the unused padding, and a recompile-time word
  (game.toml c2-60-cam-flag, launcher/crash2launcher/recompprofile.py) makes
  0x80026D04 load the crash pointer from there - 0 takes the update's own
  no-crash exit. With the mode off the flag is the pointer: the original;
- a physics-only field is drawn from a pose extrapolated from the last two
  updates by the share of a step since the last one; the real pose goes back
  at the next loop's top, so game logic only sees poses its update made. Held
  instead across a cut ("cut now" set), a jump over 2048 units or 512/4096 of
  a turn, without two consecutive steps, and after a RAM restore;
- PSX_CRASH2_60FPS_CAMERA_RATE=0 restores the per-field camera (A/B).

Heartbeat: native_60fps_camera_hz, _camera_hooked, _camera_extrapolated,
_camera_held.

tuning/native120_sim models the patched camera update: 30 updates/s at 60 and
120, drawn x and angle advancing evenly every field (through the angle wrap),
every update reading only poses it wrote, cuts and jumps held, a restore
kept, the A/B switch.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake. The game.toml change moves the
overlay config hash (d6362e32 -> 9ced4f89); both trees' caches were rebuilt.

